# {{ ansible_managed }}
# Reviewed-and-accepted scan findings. Installed once and never overwritten, so your
# edits survive `run-role.sh clamav`.
#
# Format, tab-separated:
#   <sha256>	<signature>	<path>	<yyyy-mm-dd>	<why you accepted it>
#
# Matching is on sha256 + signature ONLY. The path is a human note. That means:
#   * a file whose contents change stops matching and alerts again — swapping malware into
#     an accepted path does not inherit its acceptance
#   * a file that merely moves (a dependency version bump with identical fixtures) stays
#     accepted, with no churn
#
# Nothing is ever added here automatically. Each run writes unrecognised findings to
# new-findings.tsv with the hash already filled in; accept them deliberately:
#
#   cat ~/.clamav_automation/new-findings.tsv >> ~/.clamav_automation/baseline.tsv
#
# then add the date and reason columns by hand. If you cannot say why a finding is benign,
# it does not belong here.
